# PHP / Laravel coding style

Narrows `core-common-rules`' style rules to modern PHP (8.2+) and Laravel (11/12/13); follows PSR-12 and PSR-4. Applies only to `*.php` files.

## Naming and structure

- Constants and enum cases are `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` unless the enum case is meant to read as a label.
- Follow Laravel's default directory conventions (`app/Models`, `app/Http/Controllers`, `app/Http/Requests`, `app/Providers`, `app/Jobs`, `database/migrations`); do not invent a parallel structure.
- Keep a controller method thin: validate (Form Request), delegate to a model/action/service, return a response.
- Type-hint every parameter, property and return value that can be typed, including intersection types and `never`/`static` where they describe the contract.

## PHP 8.2+ language features

- Use `readonly` properties for value objects and anything constructed once and never mutated.
- Use native `enum` (backed by `string`/`int` when persisted to a column or API payload) instead of class constants for a fixed set of values.
- Use first-class callable syntax (`$this->method(...)`, `Str::slug(...)`) instead of string/array callables or closure wrappers.
- Use constructor property promotion for simple DTOs and services.

## Eloquent models

- Declare `protected $fillable` (allowlist) or `protected $guarded` on every model that is ever mass-assigned; do not rely on `Model::unguard()` outside a seeder/test context.
- Cast attributes with the `casts()` method (or `$casts` on codebases not yet migrated) rather than hand-parsing in accessors.
- Put the return type on relationship methods (`: HasMany`, `: BelongsTo`).

## Controllers, routes, and requests

- Use route-model binding (`Route::get('/users/{user}', ...)` with a typed `User $user`) instead of `User::findOrFail($id)`.
- Validate every request accepting user input through a Form Request (`php artisan make:request`) or `$request->validate([...])`, not raw `$request->all()`/`$request->input()` into model or database calls.
- Register route-specific middleware with `->middleware(...)`; keep global middleware in `bootstrap/app.php` (or `app/Http/Kernel.php` on older structure).

## Formatting

- Run the project's configured formatter (`./vendor/bin/pint` is Laravel's default); do not hand-format around it.
- One class per file; do not add a second top-level class/interface/enum to an existing file.
